### new InstancedMesh( geometry, material, count )

Source: https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/blob/dev/docs/pages/InstancedMesh.html

Constructs a new instanced mesh. Helps reduce the number of draw calls when rendering a large number of objects with identical geometry and material.

```APIDOC
## Constructor

### new InstancedMesh( geometry, material, count )

Constructs a new instanced mesh.

### Parameters

- **geometry** (`BufferGeometry`) - The mesh geometry.
- **material** (`Material | Array.<Material>`) - The mesh material.
- **count** (`number`) - The number of instances.

### Properties

- **boundingBox** (`Box3`) - The bounding box of the instanced mesh. Can be computed via `computeBoundingBox`. Default is `null`.
- **boundingSphere** (`Sphere`) - The bounding sphere of the instanced mesh. Can be computed via `computeBoundingSphere`. Default is `null`.
- **count** (`number`) - The number of instances. Overrides `Mesh#count`.
- **instanceColor** (`InstancedBufferAttribute`) - Represents the color of all instances. Set `needsUpdate` to true when modifying via `setColorAt`. Default is `null`.
- **instanceMatrix** (`InstancedBufferAttribute`) - Represents the local transformation of all instances. Set `needsUpdate` to true when modifying via `setMatrixAt`.
- **isInstancedMesh** (`boolean`, readonly) - Flag used for type testing. Default is `true`.
- **morphTexture** (`DataTexture`) - Represents the morph target weights of all instances. Set `needsUpdate` to true when modifying via `setMorphAt`. Default is `null`.
```

--------------------------------

### InstancedMesh: instanceMatrix needsUpdate and computeBoundingSphere

Source: https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/blob/dev/src/objects/InstancedMesh.js

The JSDoc on `instanceMatrix` warns you must set `needsUpdate` after modifying instance data. `setMatrixAt` writes to the array but does NOT set `needsUpdate` (documented as your responsibility). `computeBoundingSphere` unions each instance's transformed geometry bounding sphere; it's called lazily (e.g., on raycast) and you must call it manually after moving instances if you need an accurate bounding volume.

```javascript
/**
 * Represents the local transformation of all instances. You have to set its
 * {@link BufferAttribute#needsUpdate} flag to true if you modify instanced data
 * via {@link InstancedMesh#setMatrixAt}.
 *
 * @type {InstancedBufferAttribute}
 */
this.instanceMatrix = new InstancedBufferAttribute( new Float32Array( count * 16 ), 16 );

/**
 * Computes the bounding sphere of the instanced mesh, and updates {@link InstancedMesh#boundingSphere}
 * The engine automatically computes the bounding sphere when it is needed, e.g., for ray casting or view frustum culling.
 * You may need to recompute the bounding sphere if an instance is transformed via {@link InstancedMesh#setMatrixAt}.
 */
computeBoundingSphere() {

	const geometry = this.geometry;
	const count = this.count;

	if ( this.boundingSphere === null ) {

		this.boundingSphere = new Sphere();

	}

	if ( geometry.boundingSphere === null ) {

		geometry.computeBoundingSphere();

	}

	this.boundingSphere.makeEmpty();

	for ( let i = 0; i < count; i ++ ) {

		this.getMatrixAt( i, _instanceLocalMatrix );

		_sphere.copy( geometry.boundingSphere ).applyMatrix4( _instanceLocalMatrix );

		this.boundingSphere.union( _sphere );

	}

}

/**
 * Sets the given local transformation matrix to the defined instance. Make sure you set the `needsUpdate` flag of
 * {@link InstancedMesh#instanceMatrix} to `true` after updating all the matrices.
 *
 * @param {number} index - The instance index.
 * @param {Matrix4} matrix - The local transformation.
 * @return {InstancedMesh} A reference to this instanced mesh.
 */
setMatrixAt( index, matrix ) {

	matrix.toArray( this.instanceMatrix.array, index * 16 );
	return this;

}
```

